                                                "sense_id": "fec1b0bb-7294-3a67-a992-11b590217b03",
                                                "text": "Magic tomes […] provided access to more castable spells than would fit in most artifacts, up to two or three dozen. The military offered its soldiers a few portable arrays made of precious metals wrought into the desired shapes, but those would be even less accessible[…]"
